# Pipeline to process RiboLace data

# Step E2: UMI extraction/trimming
rule remove_linker:
Cutadapt to remove linker MC+ and following sequence from 3' end
Only reads longer than X+9 nt are retained (X is length of the RPF (usually X=20 for ribosome profiling analysis), and 9 is the sum of the lengths of the 5’ and 3’ UMIs)
-a Removal of the LACE-seq 3’ linker and any sequence that may follow
Reads in which no adapter is found are discarded

cutadapt --cores N --minimum-length X+9 -a TCTCCTTGCATAATCACCAACC --discard-untrimmed -o trim.fastq input.fastq

rule extract_umi:
UMI-tools extract to move UMI sequence to read name
Extract the first 4 (5’UMI) and the last 4 bases (3’UMI) of each read

umi_tools extract -I trim.fastq --bc-pattern='^(?P<umi_1>.{4}).+(?P<umi_2>.{4})$' --extract-method=regex -S extract.fastq --log=<umi_extract.log>

rule remove_t:
Cutadapt to remove preceding T

cutadapt --cores N -g ^T --discard-untrimmed -o trim2.fastq extract.fastq

# QC
rule fastqc:

# Step E3: Filtering rRNA, tRNA and ncRNA
rule create_contaminant_index:
Create a FASTA containing contaminating sequences from your sample
To build bowtie2 indexes fasta files of tRNAs, rRNAs and snRNAs or ncRNAs are necessary (https://rnacentral.org/)

bowtie2-build --threads N - f <reference.fasta.file> <given_index_name>

rule remove_contaminants:
Remove and quantify contaminants (rRNA, tRNA, snRNA) by aligning trimmed reads against contaminant sequences with Bowtie2 
Allows 1 mismatch (-N) 
--no-1mm-upfront - prevents Bowtie 2 from searching for 1-mismatch end-to-end alignments

bowtie2 --threads N -N 1 --no-1mm-upfront -q <trimmed.fastq.gz> --un=<norRNA.fastq.gz> -x <rRNA_bowtie_index>
bowtie2 --threads N -N 1 --no-1mm-upfront -q <norRNA.fastq.gz> --un=<norRNA_notRNA.fastq.gz> -x <tRNA_bowtie_index>
bowtie2 --threads N -N 1 --no-1mm-upfront -q <norRNA_notRNA.fastq.gz> --un=<norRNA_notRNA_noncRNA.fastq.gz> -x <ncRNA_bowtie_index>

# Step E4: STAR alignment to genome
rule create_star_index:
calculated size is 14 for hg38

STAR --runMode genomeGenerate --runThreadN N --genomeDir <location_for_index> --genomeFastaFiles <location_of_fasta_file> --genomeSAindexNbases <calculated size> --sjdbGTFfile <location_of_gtf_file>

rule star_alignment:

# Step E5: RiboWaltz pipeline
Ribosomal footprint analysis
R package that integrates QC of ribosome profiling data and P-site identification for improved interpretation of positional information
Use transcriptome BAM file and GTF annotation file to run riboWaltz (https://github.com/LabTranslationalArchitectomics/riboWaltz)

Counts

UMI-tools dedup can be used after alignment to remove duplicates based on the mapping coordinate and the UMI attached to the read name

Differentially Translated Genes - compare to DEGs
